			],
			"Message": "perf(Sky): Parallelize extension scanning, inject modulepreload hints, enable terser minification\n\nOptimise the Astro build pipeline for both developer iteration speed and production load performance.\n\n**BakeExtensionManifest — dev-rebuild debounce and parallel root scanning:**\nAdd a module-level `LastScanAt` timestamp guard so hot-reload rebuilds that fire the `astro:build:done` hook more than once within 5 s skip re-scanning the extension directories entirely, cutting repeated I/O during fast edit-save cycles. Replace the sequential `for` loop over extension roots with `Promise.all(…map(ScanRoot))` so the two extension directories are scanned concurrently, reducing single-build wall-clock time.\n\n**InjectModulePreload — new Astro build integration:**\nRegister an `astro:build:done` hook (before CompressBundle, so injected links survive compression) that parses each workbench page's `<script type=\"module\">` entry chunks, walks their `__vite__mapDeps` reference arrays plus static and (for entry chunks) dynamic import paths, and emits one `<link rel=\"modulepreload\">` hint per transitive static dep, up to 40 links per page. Without this, the WKWebView discovers the boot chain (Preload → Polyfills → Bootstrap → Workbench → SkyBridge plus their static deps) one module-graph level at a time; the hints let the browser preload the full dependency tree before execution reaches each `import()` call.\n\n**Rollup terser minification:**\nEnable `minify: 'terser'` for production builds when the VS Code workbench is not bundled into the Rollup graph (i.e. `BundledActive` is false). In bundled mode the ~44 MB `vs/**` workbench chunk would add prohibitive time and `drop_console` would strip VS Code's own diagnostics, so minification is skipped. Clarify the sourcemap comment to document why `true` is used instead of `'hidden'`: WKWebView DevTools needs the `//# sourceMappingURL=` trailing comment to discover sibling `.map` files through the `land://` static server.",
			"SHA": "64cdae903ed7825691e14f5e33543f285b44be09"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T17:35:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				154,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Sky): Expand README, add Security and Compatibility sections\n\nAdd two new reference sections to the Sky README: a Security layer breakdown covering CSP, protocol boundary, WKWebView sandbox, dependency integrity, Astro build hardening, and Tauri CSP; and a Compatibility matrix linking Sky to its sibling components (Wind, Mountain, Cocoon, Output, Worker) plus VS Code extensions and Tauri v2.\n\nAlso add an `@codeeditorland/sky` npm package badge for package-registry discoverability and a `title=\"Star\"` attribute on the GitHub stars badge image for accessibility. Remove the orphaned trailing em-quad from the System Architecture heading, which had no emoji to pair with.\n\nThese additions make the README a more complete onboarding and reference document for Sky's role in the Land editor stack.",
			"SHA": "64e3fcec5f7e37a1f8011baa92d1537a5e2425c5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T17:19:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				154,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Sky): Run SkyBridge sub-installers concurrently with error isolation\n\nRefactor `_InstallSkyBridgeOnce` in Bridge.ts so every sub-installer loads and executes concurrently instead of awaiting each in sequence, with per-installer error isolation that logs failures via `MountainIPCInvoke` without aborting the rest of the bridge setup.\n\n**Concurrent factory hydration** — Progress, Notification, Build, OutputChannels,\nand ApplyHtmlToWebview are now loaded via a single `Promise.all` call instead\nof sequential dynamic imports, reducing the time `_InstallSkyBridgeOnce` spends\nblocked on chunk fetches.\n\n**Idle-time diagnostics** — extract the two IIFE modules\n(`InstallCelDispatchTracking`, `InstallProbeServices`) from the top-level\nmodule scope into deferred functions hydrated at idle time via\n`requestIdleCallback` or a `setTimeout(0)` fallback inside\n`_InstallSkyBridgeOnce`, so their code never sits on the boot waterfall.\n\n**Parallel sub-installer batch** — wrap every bridge installer\n(EditorAndOutput, Statusbar, Commands, TasksAndDecorations, Search, Scm,\nProgressTerminalWorkspace, SimpleRelays, FanOut, Diagnostics, TreeView,\nDebug, Webview, EditorOperations, UiRequests + DeadChannelListeners) in\na `RunInstaller` thunk and run them all through `Promise.all`. One failed\ninstaller writes a `sky-bridge diagnostic:log` entry and the rest continue\nunaffected. Ordering dependencies (Statusbar's `SetOrUpdateEntry` →\nDeadChannelListeners) stay chained inside a single thunk. InstallUiRequests\nand InstallDeadChannelListeners move into this batch instead of running\nsequentially after inline completions.\n\n**Tab-flush coalescing in InstallEditorOperations** — wrap the existing\n`FlushTabs` snapshot push behind a 16ms debounce (`setTimeout`/`clearTimeout`)\nso the four events fired by a single editor tab click coalesce into one\nflush per frame. Replace the full `JSON.stringify(Snapshot)` dedupe key with\na lightweight NUL/unit-separator delimited string formed from group ids,\nactive flags, and tab label/uri pairs.\n\nSkyBridge initialization is faster, more resilient to individual installer\nfailures, and tab-snapshot IPC pushes are reduced by coalescing rapid events.",
			"SHA": "b7c70675c86e7b4f3c282b325b8cf05d3468d24d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T17:16:10Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				154,
				5
			],
			"Message": "fix(Sky): Seal SkyBridge resource lifecycle — content listener teardown, timer cleanup, and dead code removal\n\n**InstallEditorOperations — content listener lifecycle**\n  - Move `ScrollFlushTimer` outside `onDidChangeActiveCodeEditor` so teardown can clear a pending scroll flush from the previous editor before wiring the new one.\n  - Add `LastFlushedVersion` map per URI: skip the `sky:model:contentChanged` IPC round-trip when an edit or undo leaves the model version unchanged, reducing redundant full-text transmissions.\n  - Capture content listener disposables in `ContentDisposables` so they can be torn down when the editor is removed, preventing stale closures from firing into Mountain after the editor is closed.\n  - Wire `onCodeEditorRemove` to unregister all per-editor bookkeeping — pending debounce timers, version tracking, and content listener — and reset the `__celContentListened` guard so a re-added editor rewires fresh.\n\n**InstallWebview — resolveView timeout and multi-key dispose cleanup**\n  - Guard the `cocoon:request('webview.resolveView', ...)` round-trip with a 10 s timeout that resolves (never rejects) and logs a diagnostic. A hung Cocoon request must not pin the resolver past the workbench's deadline and permanently fail the view — the parked view repaints when the extension's `sky://webview/set-html` arrives.\n  - Generalise the `sky://webview/dispose` handler: accept `panelId` or `handle` from the payload, then coerce the key across string/number shapes since Mountain's emitters vary by dispatch path. Clean up three registries — `__CEL_WEBVIEW_VIEWS_BY_HANDLE__`, `PendingWebviewHtmlByHandle`, and `PendingWebviewHtml` — plus reverse-look up the viewId through `WebviewViewResolvers` to clear the by-viewId cache as well.\n\n**InstallUiRequests — timer leak fix**\n  - Capture the `window.setTimeout(…, 60_000)` return value in `FallbackTimer` instead of letting it run loose. Clear `FallbackTimer` inside `ResolveOnce` so the timeout no longer fires after a button click resolves the prompt, preventing a stray `ResolveUiRequest(RequestId, null)` from overwriting the user's choice.\n\n**InstallTreeView — remove dead code paths**\n  - Strip the four `document.addEventListener('cel:tree-view:selectionChanged|collapse|expand|visibilityChanged', …)` handlers. These `cel:tree-view:*` events are never dispatched by anyone; direct subscription to the workbench's `ITreeView.onDid*` events in the registration handler is the sole canonical path.\n  - Remove the eager `void ProvideChildren(ViewId, undefined)` call on every registration: the workbench pulls children through the attached dataProvider when the pane actually renders, so priming every registration issues a `tree:getChildren` IPC round-trip at boot for panes that may never become visible.\n  - Remove the redundant `void ProvideChildren(ViewId, undefined)` from the refresh handler: `TreeView.refresh()` already re-queries the dataProvider's `getChildren`, which re-emits `cel:tree-view:items` for Sky-side observers — calling `ProvideChildren` again doubles every `tree:getChildren` IPC.\n\n**Bridge.ts — unload guard**\n  - Add a `window.addEventListener('unload', …)` that calls `__CEL_SKY_BRIDGE_CLEANUP__` when the page unloads, ensuring bridge-side disposables are invoked even if the workbench lifecycle path doesn't reach the cleanup call in normal navigation.",
			"SHA": "16f7ac329b7c295c4544de390b2bcfaf376b1ecc"
		},
